# native_host_ffi.tkr — the NATIVE route (the default backend, no env declared) regressor for the
# aggregate-returning host FFI (0.3.1.0 degrau 34).
#
# THE EXIT NUMBER READS BACK FOUR DISJOINT WEIGHTS (4 + 8 + 16 + 32 = 60), one per host primitive
# and per branch arm: `read_file`/`env::var`/`list_dir` each take their ERROR arm and compare the
# runtime's own failure message (so a wrong out-slot pointer or length fails the compare and drops
# the weight), while `env::cwd` takes its SUCCESS arm (the working directory's `str` value marshals
# back through the same out-slots). No partial sum is 60, so any shape that mis-marshals moves the
# number and names which arm fell (`src/ffi/ffi.tks`).

Feature: native_host_ffi — the aggregate-returning host FFI lowered by the native backend

  Scenario: env::var, env::cwd, io::read_file and fs::list_dir each marshal their str/[]str-or-error result
    When built and run
    Then stdout pattern = "60"
